  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Sunday)\nIssued at 1141 AM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nLittle in the way of changes through Monday as current wave crossing \nthe Rockies steered tot he north. This will flatten the ridge enough \nto allow a potential secondary wave to bring some light precip to \nthe far western portions of the forecast area by late Monday night \nand early Tuesday. Any amounts remain light as the surface pattern \ncontinues to favor bringing dry low level air in from the east. \n\nA general breakdown in the southeast ridge is indicated by longer \nrange guidance, however any details at this point have yet to be \nresolved. Not much change in he weather anticipated until possibly \nnext weekend with warm and dry conditions. Once the current pattern \ndoes break it would likely be followed by more unsettled conditions \nand increased rain chances, though not much of an indication of a \nsignificant frontal passage at this time.",
